  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement one-by-one.\n\n- On the left of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets more and more negative, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $2.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 2\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to -\\infty \n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true while statement III is false.\n\n- On the right of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets larger and larger, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $1.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 1\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\infty \n$$\n\nTherefore, statement II is true.\n\nAs a result, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
